<title>USA: Shoreline, SJS Bancorp to merge.</title>
<headline>Shoreline, SJS Bancorp to merge.</headline>
<dateline>BENTON HARBOR, Mich. 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shoreline Financial Corp on Thursday said it plans to merge with SJS Bancorp, in a transaction valued at about $25.4 million.</p>
<p>SJS, a holding company with $151.9 million in assets, will merge into Shoreline, which has assets of $708.9 million, the firms said. SJS shareholders will receive $27 for each of their shares of SJS stock.</p>
<p>Shoreline said it expects the merger to be immaterial to 1997 net income and to enhance shareholder value in future years.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1610</p>
